  ('duck', 'HI', 'Statewide', NULL, 'no_season', NULL, NULL, 'NO DUCK SEASON EXISTS IN HAWAII - a permanent absence, not an unpublished 2026-27 date. Hawaii Administrative Rules Title 13 Chapter 122 section 13-122-4 designates 17 game birds (pheasants, quail, doves, sandgrouse, chukar, francolins, wild turkey) and lists no ducks, geese, or any waterfowl. DLNR/DOFAW''s Game Bird Hunting page lists the same species set with no waterfowl. Hawaii''s native waterfowl (koloa/Hawaiian duck, nene/Hawaiian goose) are protected. Cross-check: https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/recreation/hunting/bird/. Separately, DLNR had not posted a 2026-2027 game bird season announcement as of this fetch - the most recent on the announcements page is 2025-2026 - but that governs upland game birds, not waterfowl, which have no season regardless.', 'https://dlnr.hawaii.gov/dofaw/files/2013/09/HAR-122-Game-Birds.pdf', '2026-07-25T01:06:42Z', 'high', NULL, '1'),
