  ('duck', 'ND', 'Statewide', NULL, 'not_published', NULL, NULL, 'ND publishes ONLY start dates for 2026-27 at this time — the End Date column is blank for every waterfowl row and every row is flagged ''Tentative''. Close date is NOT published; do not infer. ND''s own table row is ''Ducks, Coots, Mergansers / Regular - Resident / High Plains Unit''. ND splits opening day by residency (resident opener is 9 days ahead of nonresident; NDGF news release notes the resident-only portion was extended from seven days to nine days in 2026). A separate ND row ''Regular - Resident/Nonresident / High Plains Unit'' starting 12/12/2026 is captured as its own record below. Also listed: ''Bonus Blue-winged Teal / All Units'' starting 09/26/2026 (bonus-bag provision, no end date published). Bag limits are not published on this page; NDGF says the 2026-27 Hunting and Trapping Guide will be available this summer. || REPAIR 2026-07-24: this record previously carried a span with close: null, which a loader cannot render. Re-verified https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/season-dates on 2026-07-24: the End Date column is STILL BLANK for every 2026-27 ND waterfowl row (ducks/coots/mergansers, Canada geese early and regular, light geese, white-fronted geese, youth, veteran) and every one of those rows is STILL labeled ''Tentative''. The page''s only finalized waterfowl row is the 2026 spring light goose conservation order (02/21/2026-05/10/2026), which belongs to the 2025-26 season. North Dakota has therefore published an OPENING date only. Per the schema, that is status=not_published with an empty dates array - not a real span with a null close. The published TENTATIVE opening date is 2026-09-26; it is preserved here in the notes on purpose and is NOT loadable season data until NDGF publishes a closing date. Do NOT infer a close date from the federal frameworks, from prior seasons, or from day-count arithmetic. NDGF footnote, verbatim: ''Note: Dates listed as TENTATIVE are subject to change until their proclamation has been signed.'' Bag limits are likewise unpublished; NDGF states the 2026-27 Hunting and Trapping Guide will be available this summer. Re-check after the proclamation is signed. || CORROBORATION 2026-07-24, four further NDGF checks, all negative: (1) the per-species pages https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/ducks and https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/canada-geese show the same blank Closes column under the header ''The dates listed below are tentative until the season''s proclamation is signed.'' Even the early Canada goose season, opening 08/15/2026, has no published close date. (2) THE PROCLAMATION IS NOT SIGNED: on https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/proclamations/archive the 2026 ''Small Game, Waterfowl and Furbearer'' entry appears as plain text with NO document link, and gf.nd.gov/gnf/regulations/docs/combination/proc-combination-2026.pdf returns 404 while the 2025 equivalent returns 200. https://gf.nd.gov/regulations/small-game still serves the 2025 proclamation, whose season dates and bag limits are 2025-26 and must NOT be carried forward. (3) NDGF news release 9128 (2026-03-23) announces openers only and states verbatim: ''The North Dakota 2026-27 Hunting and Trapping Guide will be available this summer and will provide further details on the waterfowl hunting season.'' Release 8997 (2026-01-09) states ''Dates become official when approved by governor''s proclamation.'' No 2026-27 waterfowl regulations release exists on the NDGF news index. (4) governor.nd.gov/proclamations lists no hunting proclamation at all. Zone/unit structure is unchanged for 2026-27 per release 9128: ''The zones and overall season structure for nonresident hunters will remain the same as the 2025 hunting season.'' recheck_after is set to NDGF''s historical release date for this proclamation (the prior cycle''s ''Small Game, Waterfowl, Furbearer Regulations Set'' ran Aug. 1); NDGF has published no firm commitment, so re-check repeatedly from that date rather than once.', 'https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/season-dates', '2026-07-25T01:06:11Z', 'high', '2026-08-01', '5'),
  ('goose', 'ND', 'Statewide', NULL, 'not_published', NULL, NULL, 'This record = ND''s regular Canada goose season. Start date only; End Date column blank for all 2026-27 rows. ND also lists, all Tentative and all without end dates: Canada Geese (Early Season) ''August Management Take/Early September Season'' opening 08/15/2026 in all three zones; Light Geese statewide (resident 09/26/2026, nonresident 10/05/2026); White-fronted Geese statewide (resident 09/26/2026, nonresident 10/05/2026). Bag limits not published on this page. || REPAIR 2026-07-24: this record previously carried a span with close: null, which a loader cannot render. Re-verified https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/season-dates on 2026-07-24: the End Date column is STILL BLANK for every 2026-27 ND waterfowl row (ducks/coots/mergansers, Canada geese early and regular, light geese, white-fronted geese, youth, veteran) and every one of those rows is STILL labeled ''Tentative''. The page''s only finalized waterfowl row is the 2026 spring light goose conservation order (02/21/2026-05/10/2026), which belongs to the 2025-26 season. North Dakota has therefore published an OPENING date only. Per the schema, that is status=not_published with an empty dates array - not a real span with a null close. The published TENTATIVE opening date is 2026-09-26; it is preserved here in the notes on purpose and is NOT loadable season data until NDGF publishes a closing date. Do NOT infer a close date from the federal frameworks, from prior seasons, or from day-count arithmetic. NDGF footnote, verbatim: ''Note: Dates listed as TENTATIVE are subject to change until their proclamation has been signed.'' Bag limits are likewise unpublished; NDGF states the 2026-27 Hunting and Trapping Guide will be available this summer. Re-check after the proclamation is signed. || CORROBORATION 2026-07-24, four further NDGF checks, all negative: (1) the per-species pages https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/ducks and https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/canada-geese show the same blank Closes column under the header ''The dates listed below are tentative until the season''s proclamation is signed.'' Even the early Canada goose season, opening 08/15/2026, has no published close date. (2) THE PROCLAMATION IS NOT SIGNED: on https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/proclamations/archive the 2026 ''Small Game, Waterfowl and Furbearer'' entry appears as plain text with NO document link, and gf.nd.gov/gnf/regulations/docs/combination/proc-combination-2026.pdf returns 404 while the 2025 equivalent returns 200. https://gf.nd.gov/regulations/small-game still serves the 2025 proclamation, whose season dates and bag limits are 2025-26 and must NOT be carried forward. (3) NDGF news release 9128 (2026-03-23) announces openers only and states verbatim: ''The North Dakota 2026-27 Hunting and Trapping Guide will be available this summer and will provide further details on the waterfowl hunting season.'' Release 8997 (2026-01-09) states ''Dates become official when approved by governor''s proclamation.'' No 2026-27 waterfowl regulations release exists on the NDGF news index. (4) governor.nd.gov/proclamations lists no hunting proclamation at all. Zone/unit structure is unchanged for 2026-27 per release 9128: ''The zones and overall season structure for nonresident hunters will remain the same as the 2025 hunting season.'' recheck_after is set to NDGF''s historical release date for this proclamation (the prior cycle''s ''Small Game, Waterfowl, Furbearer Regulations Set'' ran Aug. 1); NDGF has published no firm commitment, so re-check repeatedly from that date rather than once.', 'https://gf.nd.gov/hunting/season-dates', '2026-07-25T01:06:11Z', 'high', '2026-08-01', '6'),
